[objbudget]   endpoint_create at the ceiling rc=-11
[objbudget] ok - a task at its endpoint ceiling is refused with the budget's own code, not ENOMEM
[objbudget] ok - and the ceiling admitted at least one endpoint first
[objbudget]   endpoint_create after closing one rc=0
[objbudget] ok - releasing an endpoint gives its budget back to the task that created it
[objbudget]   task_create rc=0
[objbudget]   the child task's endpoint_create rc=0
[objbudget] ok - a task at its ceiling does not deny another task's endpoint_create
[objbudget]   sem_create at the endpoint ceiling rc=0
[objbudget] ok - the endpoint ceiling does not refuse a semaphore: the count is per pool
